{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally's Health and Wellness Column", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "True Stories", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the active voice when you want the 'doer' of the action to be the subject. <br/>You use the passive voice when you want the 'receiver' of the action to be the subject.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Television</span></span> (subject) <span class=\"italic\">influences<span class=\"strong\"> children's behavior </span> </span>(object).<br/>Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Children's behavior</span></span> (subject) <span class=\"italic\">is influenced by<span class=\"strong\"> television</span> (object).<br/><br/>  It is not always necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. <br/><br/>  You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the <span class=\"italic\"> to be</span> verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">am</span>/<span class=\"italic\">are</span>/<span class=\"italic\">is</span> + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The behavior of children <span class=\"strong\">is affected</span> by violence on TV.</span><br/><br/>  The Simple Past passive form is:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">was</span>/<span class=\"italic\">were </span>+ past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The behavior of children <span class=\"strong\">was affected</span> by violence on TV.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span> in the passive voice, too.<br/> You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. <br/>They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without \u2018<span class=\"italic\">to</span>') of the main verb. <br/> Modal verbs can add meaning connected with possibility, certainty or obligation.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The behavior of children <span class=\"strong\">can be affected</span> by violence on TV.</span><br/><br/>  Here the sentence now has an additional meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal verb <span class=\"italic\">can</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Many studies have been done to see whether their behavior is influenced by watching violent programs and movies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Most studies show that the behavior of children can be affected by violence on TV. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is known that young children in the U.S. watch between 25 and 52 hours of television per week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What can be done about this problem?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Organizing Points in an Argument", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use words or phrases to organize ideas in a piece of writing. Discourse markers show how ideas are connected. They usually come at the beginning of a sentence.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Discourse markers can show a <span class=\"strong\">connection</span> to what the writer is saying and what was just written. They can also show what the writer's <span class=\"strong\">opinion</span> is about what is being discussed. <br/><br/>  Look at the chart for some common discourse markers and their meanings:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Discourse Marker\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">However\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"But; contrast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Therefore\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Logical consequence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In spite of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Emphasizing a contrast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What is more\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adding\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "In spite of the violence (or maybe because of it), young kids love cartoons and prefer watching them to anything else.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What is more, it is known that young children in the U.S. watch between 25 and 52 hours of television per week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Therefore, we might be bringing up an extremely violent younger generation! ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "behavior", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way a person acts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The child's behavior started changing when he was watching cartoons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about violence on kids' television shows.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "violent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "involving the use of physical force, usually to cause damage", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Violent TV can affect children.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cartoon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an animated program, usually created for children", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The most violent programs on TV are kids' cartoons!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "rubber", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a flexible substance used to make boots, gloves, tires, etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Characters are stretched like rubber.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cliff", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a high face of a rock; a precipice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The characters are pushed over cliffs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to bring up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to educate or care for a child", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We might be bringing up an extremely violent younger generation!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to scribble", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to draw something in a careless way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The kid scribbled images of guns and blood.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "mental health", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the condition of a person's mind", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This prompted me to write about mental health challenges.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le12ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Prepare about five questions to ask your partner about cartoon violence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Consider things like: When you were a child, did you watch cartoons? What cartoons did you watch? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Spend time interviewing them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a summary of the information - use discourse markers in your writing.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I talk about cartoons and cartoon violence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about my partner's opinions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I organize my writing with discourse markers.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn8le12ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob01re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "I was talking to my neighbor the other day when she mentioned that her 10-year-old son had started to play more violent games with his friends. She also noticed that while he was doing his homework, he scribbled images of guns and blood. This prompted me to write about mental health challenges among the youth of our modern society."}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob01re2img02.jpg", "time": "18750", "id": 2, "text": "Which programs on television are the most violent? Detective series, thrillers, science fiction movies, and horror movies may all be violent, but research shows that the most violent programs on TV are kids' cartoons! In many cartoons, the characters are pushed over cliffs, stretched like rubber, run over by cars, etc. In spite of the violence (or maybe because of it), young kids love cartoons and prefer watching them to anything else."}, {"image": "engenn8le12ob01re2img05.jpg", "time": "48000", "id": 3, "text": "For many years, parents and teachers have been discussing kids and TV violence. Many studies have been done to see whether their behavior is influenced by watching violent programs and movies. Most studies show that the behavior of children can be affected by violence on TV. What is more, it is known that young children in the U.S. watch between 25 and 52 hours of television per week. Therefore, we might be bringing up an extremely violent younger generation! What can be done about this problem? Read my next entry for some ideas ..."}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le12ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le12ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about staying healthy. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what was happening when something else happened.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can organize points in an argument.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " When you were a child, did you ever watch cartoons on TV? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "  Do you think movies and TV shows for children are too violent? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Too much violence on TV?", "type": "free_type_text_a